    fix: preserve worktree assignments after cleanup

    Resolve card and project assignments by their stored branch instead of the
    position in Git's worktree list. Derive current display numbers without
    rewriting card metadata, and reserve branches by card internal ID.

    Carry expected branches through actions, schedules and Git requests. Read
    fresh registrations, verify repository and branch, and validate assignments
    before primary checkpoints. Keep conflict recovery on its captured checkout
    and allow detached HEAD only during the captured active rebase.

    Validation: 169 focused desktop tests, 248 focused app tests, app and desktop
    lint, production build, and a disposable Git cleanup reproduction. The
    broader ActionPopup file has the same two failures on base ca3ff599.

